                "styleGuidelines": "## Brand & Style\n\nThe design system is engineered for a \"cockpit\" or \"instrument\" experience, specifically tailored for a desktop-class developer utility. The brand personality is **restrained, precise, and sophisticated**, evoking the feeling of a high-end physical interface where every pixel serves a functional purpose.\n\nThe visual style is a specialized blend of **Glassmorphism** and **High-Contrast Dark Mode**. It relies on material depth rather than heavy ornamentation. Surfaces are constructed using semi-transparent layers, backdrop blurs, and fine 1px borders. The environment is grounded by a subtle radial dot grid background, creating a sense of structured space and engineering rigor.\n\nEmotional responses should lean toward focus and mastery. There is no room for illustrative fluff; quality is communicated through meticulous alignment, micro-interactions, and a luxury-tier color palette.\n\n## Layout & Spacing\n\nThe design system employs a **Fixed Sidebar + Fluid Content** layout model. The layout is rigid and grid-based to emphasize the \"cockpit\" feel.\n\n- **Sidebar:** A fixed 220px vertical column on the left.\n- **Main Stage:** A fluid area using a 32px radial dot grid as a visual guide.\n- **Grids:** Status cards and data visualizations should align to a multi-column grid within the main stage (typically 2, 3, or 4 columns depending on viewport width).\n- **Rhythm:** An 8px base unit governs all padding and margins. Vertical rhythm in the main stage is generous (32px margins) to allow the glassmorphic elements \"room to breathe.\"\n\n## Elevation & Depth\n\nThis system rejects traditional drop shadows in favor of **Tonal Layering** and **Glassmorphism**.\n\n1.  **Level 0 (Base):** Deep black `#0a0a0a` with a `dot-grid` overlay.\n2.  **Level 1 (Cards/Sidebar):** `surface-glass` (3% white) with a `backdrop-blur` of 12px-20px and a 1px `border-glass` (10% white).\n3.  **Level 2 (Overlays/Modals):** Darker glass (lower transparency, higher blur) to ensure content isolation.\n4.  **Focus Glow:** Instead of shadows, active or focused elements may emit a subtle gold glow using a soft, large-radius box shadow (`box-shadow: 0 0 60px rgba(167,139,113,0.2)`).\n\n## Components\n\n### Buttons\n- **Primary:** Solid off-white (#f5f5f4) background with dark text. 13px font size with high letter spacing. Hover states trigger a gold-tinted glow pulse.\n- **Secondary:** Transparent with `border-glass` and white text.\n- **Ghost:** No border, gold `label-caps` text for secondary actions.\n\n### Cards\n- **Status Cards:** Use a grid layout within the card. A `label-caps` gold title at the top, a 600-weight primary value in the center, and a semantic badge or grey meta-text at the bottom.\n\n### Navigation\n- **Sidebar Items:** Clear Inter typography. Active state is denoted by the primary gold color for text and a 2px vertical gold bar on the left edge.\n- **Status Capsule:** Located at the bottom of the sidebar, featuring a \"breathing\" status dot (using semantic colors).\n\n### Input Fields\n- Dark, slightly recessed background with a 1px `border-glass`. On focus, the border transitions to primary gold.\n\n### Badges\n- Pill-shaped with a 35% opacity semantic border and matching text color. Text size is strictly 10.5px.\n\n### Log Area\n- Uses a darkened background layer. Steps are colored by status (✓/✗). Step names should be highlighted in primary gold for scanability.",
